{"id": "wd-Q2665840", "status": "ok", "meta": "Titian's last painting, a Pietà meant for his own grave and left unfinished in 1576 to be completed by Palma Giovane.", "about": "Titian painted this Pietà in 1575 and 1576 and meant it to hang over his grave. He left it incomplete when he died in 1576, and an inscription at the bottom says Palma Giovane finished it. The painting was made in two stages so that it would fit in two different churches. It is now in the Gallerie dell'Accademia in Venice.", "museum_record": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AAccademia_-_Piet%C3%A0_by_Titian.jpg", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File%3AAccademia_-_Piet%C3%A0_by_Titian.jpg", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2665840", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pietà_(Titian)"], "check": "clean"}
