{"id": "cma-157681", "status": "ok", "meta": "Kubo Shunman painted Mount Fuji behind pines on the spot at a poetry club gathering, and members added humorous poems.", "about": "Kubo Shunman dashed off this loose view of Mount Fuji in the distance behind pine trees as a performance painting, called sekiga. He did it on the spot with members of his poetry club. Six of them, including the club's founder Yadoya no Meshimori, added kyoka, 31-syllable poems like waka but with a heavy emphasis on humor. Shunman wrote a poem himself in the bottom right corner, then signed and sealed the painting.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1995.18", "inventory_number": "1995.18", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "Kelvin Smith Fund", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/1995.18", "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/157681"], "check": "clean"}
